BEGIN:VEVENT
CREATED:20250311T181410Z
DESCRIPTION:$420\, 72 hrs prior to cancel for free.\nTamara - \nGary - 20
 0 - will be weighed\,\nGail - 209 - will be weighed\, intermediate\nElli
 e - beginner\nAbby - beginner\nLivy - beginner\n\nArrive 30 min prior to
  sign up and sign in.  At Colter Bay\, coming from signal it will be on 
 left and easy to see.  Comfortable clothing but closed shoes\, bug spray
 \, hat and sunscreen\, water.\nBackpacks and fanny packs\, binoculars wi
 th straps on neck not allowed.  Will have a saddle bag to put a few thin
 gs in.\n\nCheck-In\nAll guests are required to check in with one of our 
 Activities Desks at least 30 minutes* prior to an activity's departure. 
 For your convenience\, you may check in at the following locations: Jack
 son Lake Lodge Activities Desk\, Colter Bay Activities Booth\, or Headwa
 ters Lodge & Cabins Front Desk.** Each guest will be required to sign an
  Acknowledgement of Risk agreement and will receive a printed ticket.\n\
 nPlease arrive to the activity departure location (listed below) at leas
 t 15 minutes* prior to ticket time. Please note\, departure locations ma
 y be different from your check-in location and travel between locations 
 may be required. Transportation to and/or from activities is not provide
 d by Grand Teton Lodge Company or Flagg Ranch Company.\n\n**Headwaters L
 odge & Cabins guests: If you are checking in for an activity leaving fro
 m the Colter Bay Village or the Jackson Lake Lodge\, you must check in a
 t the specific location at least 45 minutes prior to your activity's dep
 arture. The Headwaters Lodge & Cabin Front Desk will ONLY check-in horse
 back rides departing from the Headwaters corrals.  \n\n*Check-in and arr
 ival times may be subject to change based on operational needs. Your pro
 perty Activities Desk has the most up-to-date information.\n\nWhat to Br
 ing\n\nFor all activities\, we recommend you bring bottled water\, sungl
 asses\, sunscreen\, hat\, camera\, layered clothing and comfortable walk
 ing shoes. Also\, be sure to bring a smile and love for adventure!\n\nSe
 e page 2 for specific departure locations and more.\n\n\nWild & Scenic R
 aft Trips\n.	Trips depart from the lower lobby of Jackson Lake Lodge.\n.
 	Guests must be 6 years of age or older\, weigh at least 50 pounds\, and
  have a chest circumference of less than 58 inches in order to wear a pr
 ovided life jacket.\n.	There is a 1/8-mile walk from the parking lot to 
 the launch site for all float trips.\n\nMarina\n.	All trips depart from 
 the Colter Bay Marina.\n.	Guests may pick up tickets and sign Acknowledg
 ement of Risk forms at the Colter Bay Marina Store/Office.\n.	For trips 
 disembarking on Elk Island\, there is a short\, uphill walk to the meal 
 site.\n.	Guided fishing prices do not include a Wyoming state fishing li
 cense\, which is required. Licenses can be purchased at Signal Mountain 
 Marina\, Headwaters Lodge & Cabins Convenience Store or at various locat
 ions in Jackson\, WY. Licenses may also be purchased online at https://w
 gfd.wyo.gov/apply-or-buy. For more info\, see https://wgfd.wyo.gov/fishi
 ng-and-boating.\n\nHorseback Riding\n\n.	Horseback riding departure loca
 tions vary by trip booked.\n.	Guests must be 8 years of age or older and
  be at least 4 feet tall.\n.	Guests under the age of 15 must be accompan
 ied by an adult 18 years or older.\n.	For the safety of our guests and h
 orses\, guests must weigh less than 225 lbs. to ride. All guests will be
  weighed at the corrals. Refunds will not be made for guests over 225 lb
 s. If you have not already provided your rider information\, please cont
 act the Activities Desk at 307-543-3299 or Reservations at 307-543-3100 
 as soon as possible.\n.	Video cameras and GoPros are not permitted on ho
 rseback rides. Cell phones are permitted but must be set to silent. Sadd
 lebags are provided for small items such as cameras\, water bottles\, an
 d binoculars. Items worn around your neck and backpacks are not permitte
 d.\n.	Closed-toe shoes and long pants are required.\n.	As a safety preca
 ution\, all guests on horseback rides must be able to show that they und
 erstand the wrangler's safety and riding instructions prior to the ride.
 \n\nBus Tours
