UID:28244
DTSTAMP:20221227T155020Z
LOCATION:Ritz Charles
DESCRIPTION:2023 IOA Winter Seminar\n\n02/08/23 08:00 AM EST\n - 02/08/23
  05:00 PM EST\nDetails:\nThe IOA's 2023 Winter Seminar will be held on W
 ednesday\, February 8\, 2023\, at the Ritz Charles\, 12156 N. Meridian S
 treet\, Carmel\, Indiana. This optometric continuing education event off
 ers seven hours of in-person IOB and Legend Drug CE credit.\n\nRegister 
 by Jan. 20 to avoid the late fee!\n\nSCHEDULE\n8:00 am – 9:00 am\nRegist
 ration and Continental Breakfast\n\n9:00 am –10:00 am \nThe Nuances of N
 ormal Tension Glaucoma\nJustin Schweitzer\, OD\, FAAO\nThe most importan
 t risk factor for glaucoma is elevated intraocular pressure\, however\, 
 the pressure theory cannot sufficiently explain how normal tension glauc
 oma causes vision loss. This course will discuss all aspects of normal t
 ension glaucoma including the pathophysiology\, diagnosis and treatment.
  1 Hour IOB and Legend Drug\n\n10:00 am – 12:00 pm\nInnovations in Glauc
 oma: Next Generation Technology\, Medications\, and Delivery\nJustin Sch
 weitzer\, OD\, FAAO\nAdvances in glaucoma diagnostics and management con
 tinue to evolve at a rapid pace. In order to continue to care for glauco
 ma patients at a high level\, it is imperative that innovation continues
  in the glaucoma space. The focus of this course is to discuss new advan
 cements in glaucoma diagnostic technology\, what’s new in the glaucoma p
 ipeline\, and what the future holds. 2 Hours IOB and Legend Drug\n\n12:0
 0 pm – 1:00 pm\nLunch included for ODs\n\n1:00 pm –3:00 pm\nVA Grand Rou
 nds\n​Anthony DeWilde\, OD\nThis course highlights the interesting\, oft
 en challenging\, patients encountered at a VA Medical Center. Various co
 nditions will be presented with an emphasis on posterior segment and sys
 temic disease. Audience participation is encouraged. 2 Hours IOB and Leg
 end Drug\n\n3:00 pm – 4:00 pm\nWhat a Pain! An Optometrist’s Guide to He
 adaches\n​Anthony DeWilde\, OD\nMany patients come to the eye doctor con
 cerned that headaches are related to their eyes. This course is designed
  to highlight important diagnostic strategies for optometrists to diagno
 se and manage patients with headaches to help determine which headaches 
 originate from ocular conditions and which headaches can have ocular man
 ifestations. 1 Hour IOB and Legend Drug\n\n4:00 pm – 5:00 pm\nSlaying th
 e Giant! Diagnosis and Management of Giant Cell Arteritis\n​Anthony DeWi
 lde\, OD\nGiant cell arteritis (GCA) is an immune-mediated vasculitis wi
 th serious ophthalmic manifestations\, including Arteritic Ischemic Opti
 c Neuropathy (AION)\, Central Retinal Artery Occlusion (CRAO)\, and dipl
 opia. It is important for the clinician to understand the signs and symp
 toms of GCA and how they relate to the eye. 1 Hour IOB and Legend Drug\n
 \nSchedule subject to change. Should any scheduling changes be necessary
 \, they will be posted on the webpage.\nAdditional Details:\nThank you f
 or registering for the IOA Winter Seminar on Feb. 8\, 2023\, at the Ritz
  Charles\, 12156 N. Meridian Street in Carmel\, IN. Registration and con
 tinental breakfast begins at 8 am\; lectures at 9 am. \n\nRefund Policy\
 nAll requests for refunds must be made in writing and must be postmarked
  or sent via email no later than Jan. 25\, 2023. Refund requests made on
  or before Jan. 25\, 2023\, will receive a full refund. Requests made be
 tween Jan. 26 and Feb. 7\, 2023\, will receive a 75% refund. No refunds 
 will be made after Feb. 7\, 2023.
SEQUENCE:0
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:2023 IOA Winter Seminar<br /><br />02/08/23 
 08:00 AM EST - 02/08/23 05:00 PM EST<br />Details:<br /><div>The IOA's 2
 023 Winter Seminar will be held on Wednesday\, February 8\, 2023\, at th
 e Ritz Charles\, 12156 N. Meridian Street\, Carmel\, Indiana. This optom
 etric continuing education event offers seven hours of in-person IOB and
  Legend Drug CE credit.<br />
SUMMARY:2023 IOA Winter Seminar
LAST-MODIFIED:20221227T205025Z
CREATED:20221227T205025Z
DTSTART:20230208T130000Z
END:VEVENT
